IMPORT prelude

-- Australian Citizenship Act 2007 (Commonwealth) -- am I a citizen, and what must I do to become one?
--
-- SEAT: the child born in or outside Australia (citizenship by birth, s 12; by descent, s 16), and the applicant for
-- citizenship by conferral (s 21 general eligibility, s 22 residence, the citizenship test, the pledge); and the citizen who
-- asks whether they could renounce (s 33). Every decision is phrased as that person asks it, from facts they could state.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: ss 2 and 4 (commencement; citizens under the old Act), s 5 (permanent resident), s 12 (citizenship by
-- birth), ss 16-19A (citizenship by descent: eligibility, the Minister's decision, registration, the day it begins), ss 20-22
-- (conferral: general eligibility under s 21(2) and (2A), the general residence requirement), s 24 (the Minister's decision),
-- s 25(3) (cancellation for want of a pledge), ss 26-28 (the pledge and the day citizenship begins), s 33 (renunciation),
-- s 46 (the fee, through the Regulation).
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 37, compilation date 4 June 2026 ("Includes amendments: Act No. 75, 2025"; register id C2026C00236),
-- as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2007A00020.txt (retrieved 2026-09-22).
-- Regulation used: Australian Citizenship Regulation 2016, Compilation No. 23, compilation date 1 July 2026 (register id
-- F2026C00596), as deposited at ../../../australian-citizenship-regulation-2016/registers/source-bundle/F2016L01916.txt
-- (retrieved 2026-10-19): s 6 (registration under s 18), s 9 (prescribed reasons for not pledging), s 10 (arrangements for the
-- pledge), s 16 and Schedule 3 (fees).
-- Also used, for the date from which s 12(1)(a) applies: Australian Citizenship (Transitionals and Consequentials) Act 2007,
-- Compilation No. 5, compilation date 1 July 2015 (register id C2015C00383), as deposited at
-- ../../../australian-citizenship-transitionals-and-consequentials-act-2007/registers/source-bundle/C2007A00021.txt, Schedule 3
-- items 1 and 4.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the Australian Citizenship Act 1948, which ss 4(2) and 5(3) make decide any question about a time before
-- 1 July 2007 (not deposited; its answers are INPUTS); ss 7-8 (ships, posthumous births, artificial conception, surrogacy);
-- ss 13-15 (adoption, abandoned children, incorporated territory); Subdivision AA (Hague adoptions); s 16(3) (births before
-- 26 January 1949); the other conferral routes in s 21(3)-(8) except as pledge exemptions and fee items; the special residence
-- and defence service requirements (ss 22A-23); s 22(4A); the content of the citizenship test (the s 23A determination is not a
-- legislative instrument and was not retrieved; passing it is an INPUT); children applying with a parent (ss 25(4), 28(3)-(4));
-- resumption (Subdivision C); revocation and cessation (ss 34-36L); evidence, personal identifiers, review, offences and the
-- regulation-making power (Parts 2 Div 4-5, Part 3); fee refunds (Regulation s 17).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill from the individual's seat with the design defaults ruled on
-- 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT for public use as advice. Dates are
-- numbers written YYYYMMDD. Judgments the Act hands to the Minister are INPUTS ("if the Minister is satisfied that ...").

§ `Australian Citizenship Act 2007`

§§ `2 and 4 -- the old Act, and who is a citizen`

-- s 2 table item 2: "Sections 2A to 54 ... A single day to be fixed by Proclamation" -- column 3: "1 July 2007 (see F2007L01653)".
-- s 3: "commencement day means the day on which sections 2A to 54 (as originally enacted) commence"; "old Act" is the
-- Australian Citizenship Act 1948 as in force before that day.
-- s 4(2): "If, under this Act, it is necessary to work out if a person was an Australian citizen at a time before the
-- commencement day, work that out under the Australian Citizenship Act 1948 as in force at that time." s 5(3) says the same of
-- permanent residence.
@export Is my citizenship at this date worked out under the Australian Citizenship Act 1948 (ss 2, 4(2))?
GIVEN `the date` IS A NUMBER @desc The date asked about, written YYYYMMDD
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my citizenship at that date a question for the 1948 Act` IF
    `the date` < 20070701

-- s 4(1): "Australian citizen means a person who: (a) is an Australian citizen under Division 1 or 2 of Part 2; or (b) satisfies
-- both of the following: (i) the person was an Australian citizen under the Australian Citizenship Act 1948 immediately before
-- the commencement day; (ii) the person has not ceased to be an Australian citizen under this Act."
-- Division 1 is automatic acquisition (s 12 among it); Division 2 is acquisition by application (descent, conferral). Ceasing
-- under Division 3 (renunciation, revocation, cessation) ends either kind.
@export Am I an Australian citizen (s 4(1))?
GIVEN `a citizen by birth under s 12` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a citizen by birth under s 12 (ask the s 12 question)
      `became a citizen by descent or conferral` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you became a citizen on application, by descent or by conferral
      `a citizen under the 1948 Act immediately before 1 July 2007` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were an Australian citizen under the 1948 Act on 30 June 2007
      `have ceased to be a citizen under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have since renounced, or had your citizenship revoked or ceased, under this Act
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I an Australian citizen` IF
        (   `a citizen by birth under s 12`
         OR `became a citizen by descent or conferral`
         OR `a citizen under the 1948 Act immediately before 1 July 2007`)
    AND (NOT `have ceased to be a citizen under this Act`)

§§ `5 -- permanent resident`

-- s 5(1): a person is a permanent resident at a particular time "if and only if: (a) the person is present in Australia at that
-- time and holds a permanent visa at that time; or (b) both: (i) the person is not present in Australia at that time and holds a
-- permanent visa at that time; and (ii) the person has previously been present in Australia and held a permanent visa
-- immediately before last leaving Australia; or (c) the person is covered by a determination in force under subsection (2)".
-- "permanent visa" is borrowed from the Migration Act 1958 and asked as a fact.
@export Am I a permanent resident for citizenship purposes (s 5(1))?
GIVEN `present in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are in Australia at the time asked about
      `hold a permanent visa` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a permanent visa at that time
      `held a permanent visa in Australia immediately before last leaving` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are abroad: whether you held a permanent visa when you last left Australia
      `covered by a s 5(2) determination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a Ministerial determination under s 5(2) covers you (special category visas, Norfolk Island, Cocos)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a permanent resident` IF
        (`present in Australia` AND `hold a permanent visa`)
    OR  ((NOT `present in Australia`) AND `hold a permanent visa` AND `held a permanent visa in Australia immediately before last leaving`)
    OR  `covered by a s 5(2) determination`

§§ `12 -- citizenship by birth`

-- s 12(1): "A person born in Australia is an Australian citizen if and only if: (a) a parent of the person is an Australian
-- citizen, or a permanent resident, at the time the person is born; or (b) the person is ordinarily resident in Australia
-- throughout the period of 10 years beginning on the day the person is born."
-- s 12(2): "However, a person is not an Australian citizen under this section if, at the time the person is born: (a) a parent
-- of the person is an enemy alien; and (b) the place of the birth is under occupation by the enemy; unless, at that time, the
-- other parent of the person: (c) is an Australian citizen or a permanent resident; and (d) is not an enemy alien."
-- Transitionals Act Sch 3 item 4(1): "Paragraph 12(1)(a) of the new Act applies to a person born on or after the commencement
-- day." Item 4(2): "Paragraph 12(1)(b) ... applies to: (a) a person born on or after the commencement day; and (b) a person born
-- before the commencement day who, immediately before that day, has not been ordinarily resident in Australia throughout the
-- period of 10 years beginning on the day the person was born."
-- s 3: "child" includes an "exnuptial child"; s 12 asks only for "a parent" and has no condition about the parents' marriage.
-- "parent", "ordinarily resident" and "enemy alien" are asked as facts.
DECLARE `Birth facts` HAS
    `born in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `date of birth` IS A NUMBER
    `a parent was a citizen or permanent resident at the birth` IS A BOOLEAN
    `ordinarily resident in Australia for the 10 years from the birth` IS A BOOLEAN
    `had completed those 10 years before 1 July 2007` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a parent was an enemy alien and the place of birth was under enemy occupation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the other parent was a citizen or permanent resident and not an enemy alien` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Am I an Australian citizen by birth under s 12?
GIVEN `my birth` IS A `Birth facts` @desc Where and when you were born, and your parents' status at the time
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a citizen by birth under s 12` IF
        `my birth`'s `born in Australia`
    AND (    (`my birth`'s `a parent was a citizen or permanent resident at the birth` AND `my birth`'s `date of birth` >= 20070701)
         OR  (`my birth`'s `ordinarily resident in Australia for the 10 years from the birth`
              AND (    `my birth`'s `date of birth` >= 20070701
                   OR  (NOT `my birth`'s `had completed those 10 years before 1 July 2007`))))
    AND (    (NOT `my birth`'s `a parent was an enemy alien and the place of birth was under enemy occupation`)
         OR  `my birth`'s `the other parent was a citizen or permanent resident and not an enemy alien`)

§§ `16, 17, 18, 19 and 19A -- citizenship by descent`

-- s 16(1): "A person may make an application to the Minister to become an Australian citizen."
-- s 16(2): "A person born outside Australia on or after 26 January 1949 is eligible to become an Australian citizen if: (a) a
-- parent of the person was an Australian citizen at the time of the birth; and (b) if the parent was an Australian citizen under
-- this Subdivision or Subdivision AA, or section 10B, 10C or 11 of the old Act (about citizenship by descent), at the time of the
-- birth: (i) the parent has been present in Australia (except as an unlawful non-citizen) for a total period of at least 2 years
-- at any time before the person made the application; or (ii) the person is not a national or a citizen of any country at the
-- time the person made the application and the person has never been such a national or citizen; and (c) if the person is or has
-- ever been a national or a citizen of any country ... and the person is aged 18 or over at the time the person made the
-- application -- the Minister is satisfied that the person is of good character at the time of the Minister's decision".
-- (The Stateless Persons Convention limb of (c) is not modelled.)
DECLARE `Descent facts` HAS
    `born outside Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `date of birth` IS A NUMBER
    `a parent was a citizen at the birth` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that parent was a citizen by descent at the birth` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that parent was lawfully present in Australia for 2 years in total before the application` IS A BOOLEAN
    `have never been a national or citizen of any country` IS A BOOLEAN
    `age at application` IS A NUMBER
    `the Minister is satisfied of good character` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Am I eligible for Australian citizenship by descent (s 16(2))?
GIVEN `my facts` IS A `Descent facts` @desc Where and when you were born, your parent's citizenship then, and your age and nationality when applying
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I eligible for citizenship by descent` IF
        `my facts`'s `born outside Australia`
    AND `my facts`'s `date of birth` >= 19490126
    AND `my facts`'s `a parent was a citizen at the birth`
    AND (    (NOT `my facts`'s `that parent was a citizen by descent at the birth`)
         OR  `my facts`'s `that parent was lawfully present in Australia for 2 years in total before the application`
         OR  `my facts`'s `have never been a national or citizen of any country`)
    AND (    `my facts`'s `have never been a national or citizen of any country`
         OR  `my facts`'s `age at application` < 18
         OR  `my facts`'s `the Minister is satisfied of good character`)

-- s 17(1A): the Minister "must not approve ... unless the person is eligible"; (2) "Subject to this section, the Minister must
-- approve the person becoming an Australian citizen if the person is eligible"; (3) not unless "satisfied of the identity of the
-- person"; (4)-(4B) security; (5) not within 12 months of ceasing to be a citizen. Unlike s 24(2) there is no power to refuse an
-- eligible applicant who clears these bars.
@export Must the Minister approve my application for citizenship by descent (s 17)?
GIVEN `my facts` IS A `Descent facts` @desc Your s 16 facts
      `the Minister is satisfied of my identity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister is satisfied of your identity
      `a security or cessation bar applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an adverse security assessment (s 17(4)-(4A)) or the 12 months after ceasing to be a citizen (s 17(5)) applies to you
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Minister approve me by descent` IF
        `Am I eligible for citizenship by descent` `my facts`
    AND `the Minister is satisfied of my identity`
    AND (NOT `a security or cessation bar applies`)

-- s 19: "A person becomes an Australian citizen under this Subdivision on the day on which the Minister approves the person
-- becoming an Australian citizen." s 19A: "Despite section 19, a person does not become an Australian citizen under this
-- Subdivision, even if the Minister approves ..., unless: (a) if the person was born on or after 26 January 1949 -- a parent of
-- the person was an Australian citizen at the time of the person's birth".
@export Am I an Australian citizen by descent on this date (ss 19, 19A)?
GIVEN `my facts` IS A `Descent facts` @desc Your s 16 facts
      `the Minister approved me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister has approved your application
      `the approval date` IS A NUMBER @desc The day of the approval, YYYYMMDD
      `the date asked about` IS A NUMBER @desc The date you are asking about, YYYYMMDD
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a citizen by descent on that date` IF
        `the Minister approved me`
    AND `the date asked about` >= `the approval date`
    AND `my facts`'s `a parent was a citizen at the birth`

-- s 18: "If the Minister approves the person becoming an Australian citizen, the Minister must register the person in the manner
-- prescribed by the regulations." Regulation s 6: "a person is registered by the Minister: (a) making a record of the fact that
-- the person is an Australian citizen by descent; and (b) including the record on a data storage system kept by the
-- Department." Registration follows approval; it is not the step that makes the person a citizen (s 19).
@export Have I been registered as a citizen by descent (s 18, Regulation s 6)?
GIVEN `the Minister approved me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister has approved your application
      `a record that I am a citizen by descent was made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a record was made that you are a citizen by descent
      `the record is on the Department's data storage system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that record is on a data storage system kept by the Department
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I been registered as a citizen by descent` IF
        `the Minister approved me`
    AND `a record that I am a citizen by descent was made`
    AND `the record is on the Department's data storage system`

§§ `21(2), 21(2A) and 22 -- conferral: general eligibility and the general residence requirement`

-- s 22(1): the general residence requirement is met if "(a) the person was present in Australia for the period of 4 years
-- immediately before the day the person made the application; and (b) the person was not present in Australia as an unlawful
-- non-citizen at any time during that 4 year period; and (c) the person was present in Australia as a permanent resident for the
-- period of 12 months immediately before the day the person made the application."
-- (1A): if "the total period of the absence or absences was not more than 12 months", the person "is taken to have been present
-- in Australia during each period of absence" -- so absences totalling MORE than 12 months save none of them.
-- (1B): for (1)(c), absences totalling "not more than 90 days", if "the person was a permanent resident during each period of
-- absence".
-- (1C): "taken not to satisfy paragraph (1)(a)" if confined in a prison, or in a psychiatric institution by court order in
-- criminal proceedings, at any time in the 4 years -- unless the Minister decides under (5A) that it would be unreasonable.
-- (2): "Paragraphs (1)(a) and (b) do not apply if the person: (a) was born in Australia; or (b) was an Australian citizen at any
-- time before the person made the application."
-- (5), (6): the Minister may treat a period PRESENT in Australia but not as a permanent resident (administrative error;
-- significant hardship) as one present as a permanent resident. (9), (11): the Minister may treat a period ABSENT from Australia
-- while a permanent resident as present as a permanent resident, for the spouse or de facto partner of a citizen (or one in an
-- interdependent relationship) who had "a close and continuing association with Australia during that period".
DECLARE `Conferral facts` HAS
    `age at application` IS A NUMBER
    `a permanent resident at application` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a permanent resident at the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
    `born in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was a citizen before applying` IS A BOOLEAN
    `absences in the 4 years before applying total more than 12 months` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an unlawful non-citizen in Australia during the 4 years` IS A BOOLEAN
    `confined in prison or by court order during the 4 years` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister decided s 22(1C) should not apply` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days present in the 12 months before applying not as a permanent resident` IS A NUMBER
    `days absent in the 12 months before applying` IS A NUMBER
    `a permanent resident during every absence in those 12 months` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister treated the present days as permanent residence under s 22(5) or (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister applied s 22(9) or (11)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister is satisfied I passed the citizenship test` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister is satisfied I am likely to reside in or keep a close association with Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister is satisfied of good character at the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
    `present in Australia at the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister is satisfied of my identity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a bar under s 24(4), (6) or (7) applies` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Do I meet the four years of presence in Australia (s 22(1)(a), (1A), (1C))?
GIVEN `my facts` IS A `Conferral facts` @desc Your residence and application facts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I meet the four years of presence` IF
        (NOT `my facts`'s `absences in the 4 years before applying total more than 12 months`)
    AND (    (NOT `my facts`'s `confined in prison or by court order during the 4 years`)
         OR  `my facts`'s `the Minister decided s 22(1C) should not apply`)

@export Do I meet the twelve months as a permanent resident (s 22(1)(c), (1B), (5), (6), (9), (11))?
GIVEN `my facts` IS A `Conferral facts` @desc Your residence and application facts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I meet the twelve months as a permanent resident` IF
        (    `my facts`'s `days present in the 12 months before applying not as a permanent resident` = 0
         OR  `my facts`'s `the Minister treated the present days as permanent residence under s 22(5) or (6)`)
    AND (    `my facts`'s `days absent in the 12 months before applying` = 0
         OR  (`my facts`'s `days absent in the 12 months before applying` <= 90 AND `my facts`'s `a permanent resident during every absence in those 12 months`)
         OR  `my facts`'s `the Minister applied s 22(9) or (11)`)

@export Do I satisfy the general residence requirement (s 22)?
GIVEN `my facts` IS A `Conferral facts` @desc Your residence and application facts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I satisfy the general residence requirement` IF
        (    `my facts`'s `born in Australia`
         OR  `my facts`'s `was a citizen before applying`
         OR  (`Do I meet the four years of presence` `my facts` AND (NOT `my facts`'s `an unlawful non-citizen in Australia during the 4 years`)))
    AND `Do I meet the twelve months as a permanent resident` `my facts`

-- s 21(2): eligible "if the Minister is satisfied that the person: (a) is aged 18 or over at the time the person made the
-- application; and (b) is a permanent resident: (i) at the time the person made the application; and (ii) at the time of the
-- Minister's decision ...; and (c) satisfies the general residence requirement ...; and (d) understands the nature of an
-- application ...; and (e) possesses a basic knowledge of the English language; and (f) has an adequate knowledge of Australia
-- and of the responsibilities and privileges of Australian citizenship; and (g) is likely to reside, or to continue to reside, in
-- Australia or to maintain a close and continuing association with Australia ...; and (h) is of good character at the time of
-- the Minister's decision". (2A): (d), (e) and (f) "are taken to be satisfied if and only if" the Minister is satisfied that the
-- person sat, was eligible to sit, started and completed in time, and successfully completed, the test approved under s 23A.
-- The special residence and defence service routes in (c) are not modelled.
@export Am I eligible for citizenship by conferral under the general criteria (s 21(2), (2A))?
GIVEN `my facts` IS A `Conferral facts` @desc Your residence and application facts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I eligible for conferral` IF
        `my facts`'s `age at application` >= 18
    AND `my facts`'s `a permanent resident at application`
    AND `my facts`'s `a permanent resident at the decision`
    AND `Do I satisfy the general residence requirement` `my facts`
    AND `my facts`'s `the Minister is satisfied I passed the citizenship test`
    AND `my facts`'s `the Minister is satisfied I am likely to reside in or keep a close association with Australia`
    AND `my facts`'s `the Minister is satisfied of good character at the decision`

-- Nothing in ss 21-28 makes giving up another citizenship a condition of conferral. (A reading of what the provisions leave out;
-- whether the other country takes its citizenship away is that country's law.)
@export Must I give up my other citizenship to become an Australian citizen by conferral?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I give up my other citizenship to be approved` IS FALSE

§§ `24 -- the Minister's decision`

-- s 24(1A): "must not approve ... unless the person is eligible"; (2): "The Minister may refuse to approve the person becoming
-- an Australian citizen despite the person being eligible"; (3) identity; (4)-(4C) security; (6) pending proceedings, prison,
-- parole and recognizance periods; (7) 12 months after ceasing to be a citizen.
-- (5): if the person is covered by s 21(2), (3) or (4), has no special residence, and "the Minister did not apply subsection
-- 22(9)" or "subsection 22(11)", "the Minister must not approve the person becoming an Australian citizen at a time when the
-- person is not present in Australia."
-- Because of (2), the most an eligible applicant can be told is that the Minister MAY approve.
@export May the Minister approve me becoming a citizen by conferral (s 24)?
GIVEN `my facts` IS A `Conferral facts` @desc Your residence and application facts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Minister approve me by conferral` IF
        `Am I eligible for conferral` `my facts`
    AND `my facts`'s `the Minister is satisfied of my identity`
    AND (NOT `my facts`'s `a bar under s 24(4), (6) or (7) applies`)
    AND (`my facts`'s `present in Australia at the decision` OR `my facts`'s `the Minister applied s 22(9) or (11)`)

§§ `25(3), 26, 27 and 28 -- the pledge and the day citizenship begins`

-- s 26(1): "A person must make a pledge of commitment to become an Australian citizen unless the person: (a) is aged under 16 at
-- the time the person made the application ...; or (b) has a permanent or enduring physical or mental incapacity ...; or (c) is
-- covered by subsection 21(6), (7) or (8)."
@export Must I make the pledge of commitment (s 26(1))?
GIVEN `my age at application` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age when you applied
      `I have a s 26(1)(b) incapacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a permanent or enduring incapacity left you unable to understand the application or show English or knowledge of Australia
      `I applied under s 21(6), (7) or (8)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you applied as a child of a former citizen, a person born in Papua, or a stateless person born in Australia
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I make the pledge` IF
        `my age at application` >= 16
    AND (NOT `I have a s 26(1)(b) incapacity`)
    AND (NOT `I applied under s 21(6), (7) or (8)`)

-- s 26(2): "A person must not make a pledge of commitment before the Minister approves the person's application ... A pledge of
-- commitment made by the person before that time is of no effect." (3)-(6): the Minister may determine that the person cannot
-- make the pledge until the end of a specified period (not more than 12 months in total); a pledge made before then "is of no
-- effect". Write 0 for `the end of any s 26(3) delay` when no determination is in force.
@export Does my pledge have effect, given when I made it (s 26(2), (6))?
GIVEN `the approval date` IS A NUMBER @desc The day the Minister approved you, YYYYMMDD
      `the pledge date` IS A NUMBER @desc The day you made the pledge, YYYYMMDD
      `the end of any s 26(3) delay` IS A NUMBER @desc The end of any period the Minister set under s 26(3) before which you could not pledge, YYYYMMDD (0 if none)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my pledge have effect` IF
        `the pledge date` >= `the approval date`
    AND `the pledge date` >= `the end of any s 26(3) delay`

-- s 27(1): "in accordance with either of the forms set out in Schedule 1" (form 1 "under God", form 2 without); (2) "in
-- accordance with the arrangements prescribed by the regulations"; (3) "before: (a) the Minister; or (b) a person authorised under
-- subsection (4); or (c) a person who is included in a class of persons authorised under subsection (5)."
-- Regulation s 10: "(a) the pledge of commitment must be made in public if it is reasonably practicable to do so; and (b) the
-- person before whom the pledge is made must read aloud the address specified in Schedule 1 to the person making the pledge."
@export Was my pledge made in the way the Act and the Regulation require (s 27, Regulation s 10)?
GIVEN `I used form 1 or form 2 of Schedule 1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you said one of the two forms of the pledge in Schedule 1 to the Act
      `made before the Minister or an authorised person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you made it before the Minister or a person (or class of persons) the Minister has authorised
      `made in public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was made in public
      `public was not reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If not in public: whether making it in public was not reasonably practicable
      `the presiding officer read the Schedule 1 address aloud` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person before whom you pledged read aloud the address in Schedule 1 to the Regulation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was my pledge made as required` IF
        `I used form 1 or form 2 of Schedule 1`
    AND `made before the Minister or an authorised person`
    AND (`made in public` OR `public was not reasonably practicable`)
    AND `the presiding officer read the Schedule 1 address aloud`

-- s 20: "A person becomes an Australian citizen under this Subdivision if: (a) the Minister decides under subsection 24(1) to
-- approve ...; and (b) if the person is required to make a pledge of commitment ... the person makes that pledge."
-- s 28(1): a person required to pledge "becomes an Australian citizen under this Subdivision on the day on which the person makes
-- the pledge"; (2) otherwise "on the day on which the Minister approves". (s 28(3)-(4), children applying with a parent, not
-- modelled.)
@export On what day do I become an Australian citizen by conferral (ss 20, 28)?
GIVEN `I must make the pledge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are required to make the pledge (ask the s 26(1) question)
      `the approval date` IS A NUMBER @desc The day the Minister approved you, YYYYMMDD
      `the pledge date` IS A NUMBER @desc The day you made an effective pledge, YYYYMMDD
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `On what day do I become a citizen by conferral` IS
    IF `I must make the pledge` THEN `the pledge date` ELSE `the approval date`

-- s 25(1), (3): the Minister may cancel an approval if the person has not become a citizen and "has failed to make a pledge of
-- commitment within 12 months after the day on which the person received notice of the approval" and "the person's reason for
-- the failure is not one that is prescribed by the regulations". (5): a cancelled approval "is taken never to have been given".
-- Regulation s 9 prescribes: (2) a s 26(3) delay determination that is in force, or ended without a reasonable period since;
-- (3) being overseas for medical treatment not available in Australia, unexpected hospitalisation, caring for a critically ill
-- person, or a funeral; (4) an administrative error or omission by the Commonwealth, a State, a Territory, an authority of any of
-- them or a local government authority. For (3) and (4) the person must still be unable to pledge, or not yet have had a
-- reasonable period to do so; and (5) the person must give the Minister "a signed statement to support the claim ..." and
-- "written evidence that supports the statement".
DECLARE `Reason for not pledging` IS ONE OF
    `no prescribed reason`
    `a s 26(3) delay determination`
    `overseas for treatment, hospitalisation, care of the critically ill or a funeral`
    `an administrative error or omission by government`

@export Do I have a reason the Regulation prescribes for not having made the pledge (Regulation s 9)?
GIVEN `my reason` IS A `Reason for not pledging` @desc Why you have not made the pledge
      `still prevented or not yet had a reasonable time to pledge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that reason still stops you, or has stopped only so recently that you have not had a reasonable time to pledge
      `gave a signed statement and written evidence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you gave the Minister a signed statement, describing your efforts to pledge, and written evidence supporting it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I have a prescribed reason for not pledging` IF
    CONSIDER `my reason`
    WHEN `no prescribed reason` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a s 26(3) delay determination` THEN `still prevented or not yet had a reasonable time to pledge`
    OTHERWISE `still prevented or not yet had a reasonable time to pledge` AND `gave a signed statement and written evidence`

@export Can my approval be cancelled because I have not made the pledge (s 25(3))?
GIVEN `I have become a citizen` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have already become a citizen under s 28
      `pledged within 12 months of notice of approval` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you made the pledge within 12 months after you received notice of the approval
      `my reason` IS A `Reason for not pledging` @desc Why you have not made the pledge
      `still prevented or not yet had a reasonable time to pledge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that reason still stops you, or you have not yet had a reasonable time since
      `gave a signed statement and written evidence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you gave the Minister a signed statement and written evidence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my approval be cancelled for not pledging` IF
        (NOT `I have become a citizen`)
    AND (NOT `pledged within 12 months of notice of approval`)
    AND (NOT (`Do I have a prescribed reason for not pledging` `my reason` `still prevented or not yet had a reasonable time to pledge` `gave a signed statement and written evidence`))

§§ `33 -- renunciation`

-- s 33(3): "Subject to this section, the Minister must approve the person renouncing his or her Australian citizenship if the
-- Minister is satisfied that: (a) the person is aged 18 or over, and is a national or citizen of a foreign country, at the time
-- the person made the application; or (b) the person was born, or is ordinarily resident, in a foreign country and is not
-- entitled, under the law of that country, to acquire the nationality or citizenship of that country because the person is an
-- Australian citizen."
-- (4): not "unless the Minister is satisfied of the identity of the person". (5): "may refuse" if the person is a foreign
-- national at application and "made the application during a war in which Australia is engaged". (6): "must not approve ... if
-- the Minister considers that it would not be in the interests of Australia to do so". (7): "must not approve ... unless the
-- Minister is satisfied that the person: (a) is a national or citizen of a foreign country immediately before the Minister's
-- decision on the application; or (b) will ... become a national or citizen of a foreign country immediately after the
-- approval." (2): the Minister must approve or refuse; where neither (3) nor a bar applies, the Act leaves it to the Minister.
DECLARE `Renunciation outcome` IS ONE OF
    `the Minister must approve`
    `the Minister may refuse`
    `the Minister must not approve`
    `the Act leaves it to the Minister`

DECLARE `Renunciation facts` HAS
    `age at application` IS A NUMBER
    `a foreign national at application` IS A BOOLEAN
    `barred from a foreign nationality because I am Australian` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister is satisfied of my identity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `applied during a war in which Australia is engaged` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister considers it not in the interests of Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a foreign national before the decision or will be one right after approval` IS A BOOLEAN

@export If I apply to renounce my Australian citizenship, what must the Minister do (s 33)?
GIVEN `my facts` IS A `Renunciation facts` @desc Your age, your other nationality, and the Minister's view of the s 33 conditions
GIVETH A `Renunciation outcome`
DECIDE `What must the Minister do if I apply to renounce` IS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `my facts`'s `the Minister is satisfied of my identity`) THEN `the Minister must not approve`
           IF `my facts`'s `the Minister considers it not in the interests of Australia` THEN `the Minister must not approve`
           IF (NOT `my facts`'s `a foreign national before the decision or will be one right after approval`) THEN `the Minister must not approve`
           IF `my facts`'s `a foreign national at application` AND `my facts`'s `applied during a war in which Australia is engaged` THEN `the Minister may refuse`
           IF (`my facts`'s `age at application` >= 18 AND `my facts`'s `a foreign national at application`) OR `my facts`'s `barred from a foreign nationality because I am Australian` THEN `the Minister must approve`
           OTHERWISE `the Act leaves it to the Minister`

-- s 33(8): "If the Minister approves a person renouncing his or her Australian citizenship, the person ceases to be an
-- Australian citizen at the time of the approval."
@export Am I still an Australian citizen on this date, having applied to renounce (s 33(8))?
GIVEN `the Minister approved my renunciation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister has approved your renunciation
      `the approval date` IS A NUMBER @desc The day of the approval, YYYYMMDD
      `the date asked about` IS A NUMBER @desc The date you are asking about, YYYYMMDD
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I still a citizen after applying to renounce` IF
        (NOT `the Minister approved my renunciation`)
    OR  `the date asked about` < `the approval date`

§§ `46 and Regulation Schedule 3 -- what my application costs`

-- s 46(1)(d) and Regulation s 16: "the fee to accompany an application under a provision of the Act is the amount set out in
-- Schedule 3". Schedule 3 (as compiled at 1 July 2026; Regulation s 19 applies the 2026 amendments to applications made on or
-- after 1 July 2026):
--   item 1: s 16 applications "made at the same time ... by 2 or more siblings": "$380 for the application by the first sibling,
--           and $160 for the applications made by the second and subsequent siblings"; item 2: any other s 16 application "$380".
--   item 21: "An application under section 33 of the Act" "$320".
@export What fee must accompany my application for citizenship by descent (Regulation Schedule 3 items 1-2), in dollars?
GIVEN `a later sibling applying at the same time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the second or later of two or more siblings applying at the same time
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the fee for my descent application` IS
    IF `a later sibling applying at the same time` THEN 160 ELSE 380

@export What fee must accompany my application to renounce (Regulation Schedule 3 item 21), in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the fee for my renunciation application` IS 320

-- Schedule 3, s 21 applications:
--   items 5-9: "Nil" (90 days' defence or pre-1964 National Service; UK or Malta child migrant wards; a re-application within the
--           window after a refusal only for residence; statelessness under s 21(8));
--   item 15: "a child, under the age of 16, who applies ... at the same time, and on the same form, as a responsible parent" "Nil";
--   item 13: claims s 21(2) and holds (or is a listed dependant on) a Commonwealth pensioner concession card: "$85";
--   item 18: claims s 21(2) and sat the test under an earlier application made on or after 1 October 2007: "$365";
--   item 14: any other s 21(2) claim: "$595";
--   item 10: does not claim s 21(2), concession card: "$40"; item 16: any other s 21 application: "$365".
--   item 17 ($40: s 21(2), earlier test, concession card) excludes "an application mentioned in item ... 13", and item 13 already
--   takes every concession-card s 21(2) application not in items 5-9 or 15; so item 17 never gives the fee (an inference from the
--   order of exclusions; see NOTES.md).
@export What fee must accompany my application for citizenship by conferral (Regulation Schedule 3 items 5-18), in dollars?
GIVEN `a nil-fee case under items 5 to 9` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a former defence or National Service member, a former child-migrant ward, a re-applicant after a residence-only refusal within the window, or stateless under s 21(8)
      `a child under 16 applying with a responsible parent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are under 16 and applying at the same time and on the same form as a responsible parent
      `I claim the general criteria in s 21(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you apply under the general eligibility criteria (and so sit the test)
      `I hold a pensioner concession card` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold, or are a listed dependant on, a Commonwealth pensioner concession card
      `I sat the test under an earlier application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you sat the citizenship test under an earlier application made on or after 1 October 2007
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the fee for my conferral application` IS
    BRANCH IF `a nil-fee case under items 5 to 9` OR `a child under 16 applying with a responsible parent` THEN 0
           IF `I claim the general criteria in s 21(2)` AND `I hold a pensioner concession card` THEN 85
           IF `I claim the general criteria in s 21(2)` AND `I sat the test under an earlier application` THEN 365
           IF `I claim the general criteria in s 21(2)` THEN 595
           IF `I hold a pensioner concession card` THEN 40
           OTHERWISE 365
